      "costUsd": 0.010824,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's a bath filling with the plug out. The tap runs in and the drain takes water out, so this graph is the net flow, twelve minus two t litres per minute, over eight minutes, with thin rectangles one minute wide. Positive means the bath is gaining water, and negative means it's losing water. The tap is being turned down, so after six minutes the drain wins, and the net flow is negative. Think for a moment. What could a strip below the axis mean? Look at the last rectangle. Its height is minus two, and its width is one minute. Minus two litres per minute, times one minute, is minus two litres. So the bath lost roughly two litres. So a strip below the axis is a negative change."
    },
