      "inputTokens": 134,
      "outputTokens": 918,
      "costUsd": 0.008329,
      "pronunciationText": "So keep every strip's sign. Strips above the axis add, and strips below the axis subtract. That makes it a signed sum. Now refine it, just as we did before. With sixteen strips, the signed sum is thirty-six. With sixty-four, it's thirty-three. With two hundred and fifty-six, it's thirty-two point two five. Now use the right ends instead. The sums are twenty-eight, thirty-one, and thirty-one point seven five. Both sets close in on the same number, thirty-two. However we choose the heights, thinner strips settle on one value."
