      "inputTokens": 200,
      "outputTokens": 1399,
      "costUsd": 0.012691,
      "pronunciationText": "That settled number gets its own name, the definite integral. We write it with this long S, which stands for sum. The integral from a to b of f of x, d x, is the limit of the sums of f of x times delta x, as delta x goes to zero. A limit is the value the sums settle on, as the strips get thinner. The d x reminds us of the strip width, and a and b are the ends of the interval. The units come along too. Litres per minute, times minutes, gives litres. And this works for any rate. The sums estimate the total change, so their limit is the total change itself. For the storm in the last video, it's the rain that fell. For this bath, it's the change in the water it holds. Here, the integral from zero to eight of twelve minus two t, d t, looks like thirty-two. Let's check that with shapes."
    },
