      "costUsd": 0.0047605,
      "pronunciationText": "When the graph makes simple shapes, we can find the integral from their areas. From zero to six, the graph and the axis make a triangle, with base six and height twelve. Half of six, times twelve, is thirty-six. So the integral from zero to six is thirty-six, and the bath gains thirty-six litres."
