      "pronunciationText": "Over the whole eight minutes, the graph changes sign. The integral adds the signed pieces. Thirty-six, plus minus four, gives thirty-two. That matches the settled sums. It's the net change: the bath ends with thirty-two litres more than it started with. If it had drained more than it gained, the integral would be negative. Area above the axis counts as positive, and area below counts as negative."
