      "pronunciationText": "The shape doesn't have to start at zero. Find the integral from one to three of two x plus one. At x equals one, the line is at height three, and at x equals three, it's at height seven. The region between the line and the axis, from one to three, is a trapezium. Its area is the average of three and seven, times the width two, which is ten. The graph stays above the axis, so the integral is ten."
