      "pronunciationText": "Here's a surprise. Find the integral from minus three to three of x. From minus three to zero, the line is below the axis, making a triangle with area four and a half. From zero to three, there's a matching triangle above, also four and a half. So the integral is four and a half, minus four and a half, which is zero. There's plenty of area here, but the integral is zero, because the part above and the part below balance."
