      "pronunciationText": "Sketch it first. At zero the line is at minus five, and at three it's at minus two, so it's below the axis the whole way. The shape is a trapezium, with parallel sides five and two, and width three. Its area is three, times seven over two, which is twenty-one over two. It's below the axis, so the integral is minus twenty-one over two. Twenty-one over two is wrong. It loses the sign."
